{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /8}3{csc}^{2}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}3{csc}^{2}⁡(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(u))\\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(0+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553529 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553400 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553529 #edb/ref 1069 "q-224529" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553529 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553529 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.26)$ given below, compute $P(3<X\\le 5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.1642\\,$ | $\\,0.5104\\,$ | $\\,0.8144\\,$ | $\\,0.9569\\,$ | $\\,0.9944\\,$ | $\\,0.9997\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\n$P(3<X\\le 5)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553529 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "63f99f88-8f04-51ab-8690-7dde4f450856" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553529 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3\\})+P(X\\in \\{4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 3)+P(3<X\\le 5) \\\\  & =F(3)+P(3<X\\le 5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<X\\le 5) & =F(5)-F(3) \\\\  & =0.9997-0.9569 \\\\  & =0.0428.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553596 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186553650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553596 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0ab744e4-bdf5-5945-9358-bad084def263" #edb/ref 175921